WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.710 align:start position:0%
 
not long after the release of the  division  in 2016 it was announced that there is  an action feature film adaptation in  development  starring jack gillenhall and jessica  chastain  but over time this seemed to fall off  the radar with no updates over the  following years  most fans had come to the conclusion  that the movie had been shelved  however out of the blue five years after  the initial announcement  we were given news that not only is the  film currently being worked on  but it's being led by a new director who  just happens to be  a huge fan of the franchise  originally i wasn't going to talk about  this because it was plastered all over  social media and i figured a lot of  people were probably already quite aware  but i was still getting a ton of  questions in the youtube comments which  started to highlight that  not everyone is as nerdy as me checking  out all the latest media updates  and following all the social circles so  that plus the fact that my channel is  heavily invested in the story and  setting of the division universe  it probably makes sense that i cover  this  when the idea of the movie was first  announced david leach was put in place  as the director but over time he was  forced to step into a producer role due  to scheduling conflicts  and this is where rawson thurber took  the reins  gerber's most recent work includes the  action comedy thriller red notice  where he wrote and directed the film  starring dwayne johnson  and ryan reynolds due to be released  sometime in 2021  previously he's worked on other movies  such as skyscraper central intelligence  dodgeball and weather millers  shortly after it was announced on  twitter day one community member and  host of the echocast podcast  born diesel asked if thurber would like  to have a chat on a show  and i gather much to born surprise he  accepted  thurber has been a day one fan of the  division franchise and actually waited  for three hours in line to watch it at  e3  2013 when it was first announced he  spoke about how the first time he saw  the game his jaw was on the floor  the attention to detail the atmosphere  the impressive graphics  and the dark and gritty feel around a  christmas that was never able to happen  since the release of the division one  thurber himself has invested many  thousands of hours of game time into the  franchise  now obviously there is only so much he  could talk about regarding the story  but he did make some interesting  comments on the parts of the division  story that has motivated the direction  he'd like to take the movie  the concept of the division one  particularly appeals to him because it's  fundamentally about doing something good  getting the power back on getting food  to people and helping others  he goes on to talk about how the  division is not a post-apocalyptic  story it's a mid-crisis story while  society is bouncing on a knife's edge  it's up to us to save it there are also  a lot of questions  like what do we owe each other in a  society in a lawless state where there  is no  external force it's basically up to your  own moral compass to make the choice  whether you want to help or become a  part of the chaos unfolding around you  what would you do when everything falls  apart  another unique aspect is that the  division agents are essentially normal  people  they come from all walks of life but  when that watch is activated  they pack their things and run towards  the danger  this adds a powerful supporting theme  for the story  obviously there will be a lot of action  shooting and taking cover  but what it's really about is supporting  those who can't support themselves  so in case it wasn't obvious by now the  movie will be set in new york  and will be based around the same time  period as the division one  and before you ask yes the hunters will  be making an appearance  one of the first things people talk  about when they hear of the division  becoming a film  is that movie adaptations based on video  games don't exactly have the best  reputation  more often than not they either aren't  particularly good or they don't perform  well  and thurber is well aware of this but he  goes on to explain  about how the division is a little  different to other films that have been  made in the past  firstly although there are a number of  well-known characters like feylau  benitez keener etc  the main character the player agent you  play as yourself  you experience the division as yourself  he is also very adamant on the fact that  the way you experience a video game is  very different to the way you experience  a film  and that you should never try to make a  movie that feels like a video game  or vice versa a video game like a movie  thurber's plan is to approach the movie  by telling a story  that is set within this world that feels  like a division story  and is about those characters and their  journey  there will be a ton of easter eggs  weapons and shooting as this is very  important  but the story and the characters need to  be front and center  in saying that thuba has stated that the  skills must be included  that they are a huge iconic part of the  division there may not be room for all  of the skills but the ones mentioned  were sycamines  pulse turrets both flame and assault and  a hive  he seems quite passionate about this  aspect in fact in his words he said  what's so awesome about the division is  the tech i'm going to be shameless about  using as much of it as i can  so it'll be quite interesting to see how  these turn out  for a movie based on a video game to  succeed it needs to appeal to an  audience far wider than the player base  itself  thurber is taking the opportunity to  tell a story that's fresh  and feels of the game but at the same  time isn't just  the game he wants the story and movie to  lean on the fundamental questions  of what do we owe each other in society  what are you willing to do  to save what you love how will we help  each other during these times  are you a selfish person or a selfless  person in these moments of crisis  the movie is currently in the scripting  phase there was a previous draft but  thurber had a very specific idea of what  he wanted to do  so he started from scratch with writer  alan shenman  once the script is done and approved the  pre-production of the movie will begin  if all goes well they're hoping to start  shooting by the end of 2021  jake gyllenhaal and jessica chastain are  very focused and passionate on this  movie and are pushing to start the  shooting as soon as possible  so fingers crossed we'll be seeing some  more progress by the end of the year  rawson thurber described his ambitions  behind this film as an attempt to show  an exciting and harrowing  story full of jeopardy heart and a touch  of humor to top it off  a big thank you to born diesel for not  only being more than happy with me using  the information from his ecocast  interview  but for reaching out on behalf of the  division community to have a chat about  the intentions towards something that  many of us hold very close to our hearts  please check out borne's channel and  show out some engie and love  spam those comments for me you won't  find too many other people as dedicated  as him when it comes to the division  franchise  i'll also have a link to the full 40  minute interview in the description  also if for some weird reason that  rawson watches this video  thank you i'm glad that this movie has  been put in the hands of someone who's  obviously a fan of the game  admittedly i always thought the division  story would make a decent movie  however i wasn't particularly  enthusiastic about it  but now with a member of this odd little  community at the helm  i'm very excited to see the outcome no  pressure  anyway thank you very much for watching  everyone i hope you found this  informative  and i'll catch you in the next one  [Music]  cheers  [Music]  uh

